  "Give it a name": "Donnez un nom",
  "A bit bigger, please — draw that one again.": "Un peu plus grand s'il vous plaît — recommencez.",
  "Straight lines are taken as scrolling. Draw a shape with a turn in it.": "Une ligne droite compte comme un défilement. Faites un angle ou une courbe.",
  "Got it. Again.": "Bien reçu. Encore.",
  "Looks distinct from the other gestures. Save it.": "Se distingue bien des autres gestes. Enregistrez.",
  "Saved, but it can't be used with one finger: it isn't a closed shape": "Enregistré, mais inutilisable à un doigt : forme ouverte",
  "A cross is two quick diagonal strokes, which is exactly what two flicks look like while scrolling a feed or moving a map. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Une croix ressemble à deux balayages rapides ; à un doigt elle se déclencherait toute seule.",
  "This is two straight lines with one corner. Ordinary drags, swipes between photos and the back gesture draw that shape all the time, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Deux droites avec un angle ressemblent trop aux gestes retour ou photo habituels.",
  "Part of this digit is an open line, and a scroll that curls at the end can look just like it. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Une partie de ce chiffre est ouverte et ressemble à un défilement courbé.",
  "A one-finger swipe is how every app scrolls.": "Glisser à un doigt sert à défiler dans toutes les apps.",
  "This digit is an open line that doesn't end where it starts. A curved scroll or swipe in an app can draw the same shape, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Ce chiffre ne se ferme pas au départ et pourrait se déclencher en défilant.",
  "With one finger only closed shapes are allowed (one stroke that ends where it started), because ordinary scrolls and swipes never do that. This custom gesture isn't drawn that way.": "À un doigt, seules les formes fermées sont permises (un trait qui revient au départ).",
